  },
  {
    "insert": "Weakness:",
    "attributes": {
      "bold": true
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "\nThe motivation should explain to the reader why the chosen topic is relevant and which weakness the thesis wants to address. Although the basic problem is introduced in your synopsis, the current approach could be explained more clearly. To do this, read the current literature again and summarise in a short section how it is currently dealt with."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": " It is very important to make it clear in an exposé what the aim of the work is in order to give the reader a precise understanding of the objectives. Your research questions could be formulated more precisely. They seem a little unclear and need to be better formulated so that the reader understands exactly what the study is trying to investigate. Read through your research questions again and try to formulate them more clearly. If you need inspiration, take a look at research questions from various theses."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The state-of-the-art should position your work against existing reasearch. Your SOTA section is incomplete and the problem is not fully clarified. In your text, try to explain the current weaknesses in current research in more detail. "
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The methodology describes how the individual research questions will be answered. Your methodology is generally very well structured, but you should still address the limitations and challenges of your methodology. To do this, consider what difficulties the individual methods may involve. You can research the disadvantages of these methods."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The time schedule is used to plan the thesis in advance to see whether it is possible in the short time available. It is therefore very important that all aspects of the thesis are included. The writing of the thesis and the submission are missing in your time schedule. Think about which chapters all belong in a thesis and when they should best be written. Additionally, a buffer period should be at the end of the schedule to account for unforeseen delays, which is vital for proper project planning."
  },
